<title>FINLAND: Finnish PM confident EMU will start on schedule.</title>
<headline>Finnish PM confident EMU will start on schedule.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1996-12-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Finnish Prime Minister Paavo Lipponen said on Thursday it was extremely likely that the third stage of Europe's Economic and Monetary Union would start as scheduled on January 1, 1999.</p>
<p>&quot;Yes, it is now after Dublin more than highly likely that it will come true,&quot; Lipponen told Reuters when asked if the third stage of EMU would happen after EU leaders agreed on a stability pact last weekend in Dublin.  </p>
<p>Lipponen also said the stability pact was considered a good step in bolstering the credibility of Europe's planned new currency, the euro.</p>
<p>-- Helsinki newsroom +35 89 6805 0247</p>
</text>
